## 4.1.0 (2026-08-25)

### New feature:

-   renamed to Gloss, with a new icon drawn for it
-   glossary: terms you want rendered a particular way, scoped by language pair. LLM services get them as an instruction so the model applies them while translating; every other engine has them applied to the result
-   in-place image translation on Linux, via tesseract TSV output (it was Windows only)
-   a test suite, run on every PR

### Improved:

-   both translate paths now share one dispatch, so a change to how a translation is prepared has one place to go
-   service settings forms are built from shared parts, and all 43 are covered by a test
-   faster Ctrl+C selection, and one less window flashing on Windows
-   the translate window opens at 440x580

### Bugs fixed:

-   in-place image translation painted the literal string `[STREAM]` over the image, and cached it
-   `http://*` in the capability scope matched only the protocol's default port, which broke the Recognize window's translate button, the Anki collection service on 8765, and every self-hosted endpoint
-   toasts drew the library's white default under a dark theme, and a page with a modal open drew each toast twice
-   the tray icon was the full-colour app icon with `iconAsTemplate` set, which macOS reduced to a filled black square in the menu bar
-   selection COM and clipboard fixes, and a Linux session with no `XDG_SESSION_TYPE` no longer fails to read the selection
-   ChatGLM now goes through the plugin's fetch, so the proxy setting reaches it
